"answer": "Project Zenith is a new data analytics initiative aimed at revolutionizing the company's approach to data analytics. The project was introduced by Alex with a kick-off on June 15th and an initial budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The team expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. In July, Emily called for R&D proposals to leverage AI for data visualization tools. The budget was later adjusted to $550,000 by Jordan to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration, while Carla noted a $55,000 budget increase for the compliance plan. Neil reported significant progress in Phase Two, specifically a breakthrough in predictive analytics, with a detailed report due on November 20th. The launch date is set for March 15, 2024. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, will be updated starting January next year. Additionally, the company is exploring a partnership with TechInnovate for AI technology. A separate onboarding session for 'Zenith Innovations' (a partner or related entity) was scheduled for April 15, 2023."
